      "description": "Habitans de l'île de Pasques: \nPrint. Portrait of a man and a woman, inhabitants of Easter Island. A woman, on the left, wears a cloth wrap skirt. The man, on the right, has tattoo markings on his face, arms and legs and wears a cloth cloak, and plant leaf loin cover, and plant leaf hair ornament. Banana plant in the background. 1822.\nLithograph, printed in borwn, yellow and green tones\nPrint made by: Ludwig Choris; Printed by: Langlumé.\nPublished in: Choris, Louis (1822) \"Voyage pittoresque autour du monde: avec des portraits de sauvages s'Amerique, d'Asie, a'Afrique, et des iles du Grand Ocean/ des paysages, des vues maritimes, et plusieurs objets d'histoire naturelle\".\n\nIt is believed that this print was bound together (see holes on side and/or top of print) alongside other prints by Louis Choris, which are now part of the BM Pictorial Collection.",
